<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Dutch authorities seize 26 critically endangered turtles from luggage of passenger bound for Hong Kong</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:880177184aa49ef09c0efa88143a581d4d36f1e05377265c4700f7a425f0142e</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:19Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T15:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-ko/a-80077824--bdef9f0677e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/dutch-authorities-seize-26-critically-endangered-turtles-from-luggage-of-passenger-bound-for-hong-kong/a-80077824?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The tiny Vallarta mud turtle was only discovered in 2018. It's critically endangered with around 300 thought to live in the wild. Almost one tenth of that number were stashed in a traveler's luggage, bound in duct tape.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Arsenic in the water: Thailand presses Myanmar over mining pollution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:499df7c102acb1d8768369cae7abec58c8874d7e3164f0e603807fb066febbc2</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:22Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/arsenic-in-the-water-thailand-presses-myanmar-over-mining-pollution/a-80074295--98cdabbb5354.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/arsenic-in-the-water-thailand-presses-myanmar-over-mining-pollution/a-80074295?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Thailand is seeking to tackle river pollution stemming from rare earth mines in neighboring Myanmar. The two countries held joint talks this week as a "first step towards agreeing on the evidence."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Duterte's ICC trial: What is at stake for the Philippines?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3b1f38ba4c361f2be0980d99633bcd100ba3a64ac80c983ed623a8ebef122db</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:41Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T13:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657--9d6c676a2419.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/duterte-s-icc-trial-what-is-at-stake-for-the-philippines/a-80075657?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte faces trial in The Hague over his deadly war on drugs. The proceedings could also determine the political fortunes of one of the Philippines' most powerful dynasties.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines: VP Duterte says father's ICC case 'not a fair trial'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b754f7324e8a37cab0752ccf75cb818164fbcea4cd78ad4201bcdf5a27b46a1</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:47Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-vp-duterte-says-father-s-icc-case-not-a-fair-trial/a-80074359--fe3a5d80492d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-vp-duterte-says-father-s-icc-case-not-a-fair-trial/a-80074359?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sara Duterte has said the ICC will not give her father a fair trial and that the Hague-based court wants to "make a statement." Duterte alleges the case against her father is politically motivated.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How East Germany boosted Vietnam's coffee industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:57cca87618bc43bd2827b6c602defe90594bc43dcbc6c1f0facaae7eaa80264d</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:18:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T12:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-east-germany-boosted-vietnam-s-coffee-industry/a-80029974--4f080bc8669e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-east-germany-boosted-vietnam-s-coffee-industry/a-80029974?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">When East Germany could no longer afford to import coffee, it introduced a substitute blend containing rye and chicory in 1977. A public outcry ensued. The solution to the problem lay 9,000 kilometers away — in Vietnam.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>India's Modi government calls special sitting of parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:975481c8f0c1ea2145e0e7840278f128f9a2dc9bc2d0f3c4e069a8542af16aca</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:19:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-27T07:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-modi-government-calls-special-sitting-of-parliament/live-80070511--c4ca03e24929.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-modi-government-calls-special-sitting-of-parliament/live-80070511?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sitting of the Indian parliament comes after its monsoon session was adjourned indefinitely in August.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Is authoritarian Vietnam ready to phase out the death penalty?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d0c939e71f0f8ffbec7f47f7ce174665fb83b60148f7adb32c0d26d5d90bd1b9</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T15:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-authoritarian-vietnam-ready-to-phase-out-the-death-penalty/a-80064271--09c5b90052b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-authoritarian-vietnam-ready-to-phase-out-the-death-penalty/a-80064271?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vietnam has voted to abolish the death penalty for six more crimes, continuing a decades-long trend of restricting capital punishment.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU-Indonesia trade deal opens new markets, but challenges remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1dc2d7e7304182c9638253e317302822da524cd740d1241e5d70fe82584304dd</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T13:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568--6d93bfcf9a92.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-indonesia-trade-deal-opens-new-markets-but-challenges-remain/a-80059568?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The agreement offers new export and investment opportunities for Jakarta and Brussels. But can Indonesia turn Europe's growing interest in its markets and critical minerals into sustainable gains at home?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Resolve tariff concerns in trade talks — India tells US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9af35e1afaa8ff050ae4ecbfbb8604a038751973f23ce6c1d581eef41058a34c</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T06:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-resolve-tariff-concerns-in-trade-talks-india-tells-us/live-80056202--8adafaf8404f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-resolve-tariff-concerns-in-trade-talks-india-tells-us/live-80056202?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">India has denied US claims that New Delhi's policies promote excess manufacturing capacity. Further headlines from India include Constitution Day celebrations. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How Chinese companies circumvent chips sanctions in Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0936376b57468a71fb9b09975d53478da475e6c607a73c3fe0c1ec50404a0366</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T06:11:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-chinese-companies-circumvent-chips-sanctions-in-southeast-asia/a-80041002--ca78b0ef9d25.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-chinese-companies-circumvent-chips-sanctions-in-southeast-asia/a-80041002?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">High-tech AI chips are hard to get in China because of US restrictions. To get around this, Chinese companies often use offshore computing capacity, particularly in Southeast Asia. The US is also trying to stop it.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kim Jong Un tours nuclear material sites, urges wider use of tactical nuclear weapons</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:623e2bd303617c2c7c6b4ad7e068f1a34e335e5a79a0e6b49bbce744df98ac4a</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-26T04:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kim-jong-un-tours-nuclear-material-sites-urges-wider-use-of-tactical-nuclear-weapons/a-80055887--3e6bd65b24cc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kim-jong-un-tours-nuclear-material-sites-urges-wider-use-of-tactical-nuclear-weapons/a-80055887?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korea's Kim Jong Un visited sites that produce nuclear material and told his military to focus on tactical weapons, saying his country's nuclear status is irreversible.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Indian nationals are still ending up in Russia's war on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bae444b74fa5554df4aaff9a26544a7e1ffe1b09f7ce9054ef46d3d17dbf9de0</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537--f2a88cb80a6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Whether through deception or desperation, Indians continue to be drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine. What can New Delhi do to protect its citizens from ending up fighting in Ukraine?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Afghanistan, no female doctor often means no treatment for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ad5167b383f10ee0982bdc083085ecd12441d4d42f8f6136834c29b00e27400</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053--cac71a2a15bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Millions of women in Afghanistan, particularly pregnant women, are suffering under Taliban restrictions and are increasingly losing access to life-saving medical care.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Deepfakes and 'US abandons Taiwan' claims spread ahead of vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bd7b7b86b9591261527ffdf67165ccd4d5fbc97b0f4cd097bd5904a7384c8759</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834--56b12ab42141.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of local elections, Taiwan is seeing a surge in AI-generated attacks on mayoral candidate Puma Shen, alongside disinformation portraying the US as abandoning the island.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b5d9b6125e17cd56fed8a63c7ad246e37603a64e80263920b52a1073cd3a2152</id><updated>2026-11-27T18:17:40Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
